            <ArticleTitle>Epidemiology of chronic facial pain: diagnostic usefulness in patient care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1604-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three chronic facial pain conditions--temporomandibular pain and dysfunction syndrome, phantom tooth pain and burning mouth syndrome--can puzzle dentists trying to provide diagnoses and treatment plans. Epidemiologic data and their usefulness in providing diagnostic criteria for these conditions are explored.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
